# Procedural Generation Guidelines

## Overview

This document provides guidance for implementing procedural content generation in BrogueMCP, focusing on dungeon generation, entity placement, and environmental features.

## Core Principles

### Seed-Based Generation

All procedural generation should be deterministic based on a seed value:

```c
typedef struct DungeonGenContext {
    unsigned int seed;           // Master seed for this dungeon
    int dungeonLevel;            // Current depth level
    unsigned int regionSeeds[4]; // Derived seeds for different generation phases
    // Other generation parameters
} DungeonGenContext;

void initDungeonGenContext(DungeonGenContext* context, unsigned int seed, int level) {
    context->seed = seed;
    context->dungeonLevel = level;
    
    // Create derived seeds for different aspects of generation
    // Using different seeds for different generation phases prevents
    // changes to one phase from affecting others
    unsigned int derivedSeed = seed + (level * 17);
    context->regionSeeds[0] = derivedSeed * 104729; // Room generation
    context->regionSeeds[1] = derivedSeed * 104743; // Corridor generation
    context->regionSeeds[2] = derivedSeed * 104759; // Feature placement
    context->regionSeeds[3] = derivedSeed * 104761; // Monster/item placement
}
```

### Layered Generation Approach

Break generation into distinct phases that build upon each other:

1. **Terrain Generation**: Create the basic dungeon layout
2. **Feature Placement**: Add special features (traps, altars, etc.)
3. **Item Placement**: Distribute items throughout the dungeon
4. **Monster Placement**: Position monsters based on difficulty and theme

### Modularity

Design generation algorithms to be modular and composable:

```c
// Generation phases - each function handles one aspect of generation
void generateBaseTerrain(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void placeRooms(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void createCorridors(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void addWater(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void addVegetation(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void placeItems(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);
void placeMonsters(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map);

// Main generation function
DungeonMap* generateDungeon(unsigned int seed, int level, GenerationParams params) {
    DungeonMap* map = createEmptyMap(params.width, params.height);
    if (!map) return NULL;
    
    DungeonGenContext context;
    initDungeonGenContext(&context, seed, level);
    
    // Execute generation phases in sequence
    generateBaseTerrain(&context, map);
    placeRooms(&context, map);
    createCorridors(&context, map);
    
    // Environmental features
    addWater(&context, map);
    addVegetation(&context, map);
    
    // Content
    placeItems(&context, map);
    placeMonsters(&context, map);
    
    return map;
}
```

## Dungeon Structure Generation

### Room Generation

Create varied room types with different shapes and characteristics:

```c
typedef enum RoomType {
    ROOM_RECTANGULAR,
    ROOM_CIRCULAR,
    ROOM_CROSS,
    ROOM_CAVE,
    ROOM_SPECIAL
} RoomType;

typedef struct Room {
    RoomType type;
    int x, y;             // Top-left corner
    int width, height;    // Dimensions
    int connections;      // Number of connections to other rooms
    bool hasSpecialFeature;
    // Additional properties
} Room;

Room* generateRoom(DungeonGenContext* context, RoomType type) {
    Room* room = malloc(sizeof(Room));
    if (!room) return NULL;
    
    room->type = type;
    
    // Determine size based on room type
    switch (type) {
        case ROOM_RECTANGULAR:
            room->width = randomInt(5, 12);
            room->height = randomInt(5, 9);
            break;
        case ROOM_CIRCULAR:
            room->width = room->height = randomInt(5, 10) | 1; // Ensure odd number
            break;
        // Handle other room types
    }
    
    // Additional room setup
    room->connections = 0;
    room->hasSpecialFeature = randomChance(0.15f);
    
    return room;
}
```

### Corridor Generation

Connect rooms with corridors, ensuring a navigable dungeon:

```c
bool connectRooms(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map, Room* roomA, Room* roomB) {
    // Get connection points from each room
    Point pointA = getConnectionPoint(roomA);
    Point pointB = getConnectionPoint(roomB);
    
    // Create corridor path
    if (randomChance(0.5f)) {
        // L-shaped corridor
        createHorizontalCorridor(map, pointA.x, pointB.x, pointA.y);
        createVerticalCorridor(map, pointA.y, pointB.y, pointB.x);
    } else {
        // Alternative L-shaped corridor
        createVerticalCorridor(map, pointA.y, pointB.y, pointA.x);
        createHorizontalCorridor(map, pointA.x, pointB.x, pointB.y);
    }
    
    roomA->connections++;
    roomB->connections++;
    
    return true;
}
```

### Map Connectivity

Ensure the dungeon is fully connected and accessible:

```c
bool ensureConnectivity(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map, Room** rooms, int roomCount) {
    // Create a graph representation of room connections
    Graph* connectivity = createGraph(roomCount);
    
    // Add existing connections to the graph
    for (int i = 0; i < roomCount; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < roomCount; j++) {
            if (areRoomsConnected(map, rooms[i], rooms[j])) {
                addEdge(connectivity, i, j);
            }
        }
    }
    
    // Find disconnected components
    int* components = findConnectedComponents(connectivity);
    int componentCount = countUniqueComponents(components, roomCount);
    
    // Connect disconnected components
    while (componentCount > 1) {
        // Find two rooms from different components
        int roomA = -1, roomB = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < roomCount; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < roomCount; j++) {
                if (components[i] != components[j]) {
                    roomA = i;
                    roomB = j;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (roomA != -1) break;
        }
        
        // Connect these rooms
        connectRooms(context, map, rooms[roomA], rooms[roomB]);
        
        // Update connected components
        free(components);
        components = findConnectedComponents(connectivity);
        componentCount = countUniqueComponents(components, roomCount);
    }
    
    free(components);
    destroyGraph(connectivity);
    
    return true;
}
```

## Environmental Feature Generation

### Water Features

Generate lakes, rivers, and pools:

```c
void addWater(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Decide on water feature type based on dungeon level
    float riverChance = 0.3f - (context->dungeonLevel * 0.02f);  // Less rivers at deeper levels
    float lakeChance = 0.2f + (context->dungeonLevel * 0.01f);   // More lakes at deeper levels
    
    if (randomChance(riverChance)) {
        generateRiver(context, map);
    }
    
    if (randomChance(lakeChance)) {
        generateLake(context, map);
    }
    
    // Always add some small water features
    int poolCount = randomInt(2, 5);
    for (int i = 0; i < poolCount; i++) {
        generatePool(context, map);
    }
}

void generateRiver(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Start from one edge of the map
    int startX, startY, endX, endY;
    
    // Determine river start and end points
    if (randomChance(0.5f)) {
        // Horizontal river (north to south or south to north)
        startX = randomInt(map->width / 4, map->width * 3 / 4);
        startY = (randomChance(0.5f)) ? 0 : map->height - 1;
        endX = randomInt(map->width / 4, map->width * 3 / 4);
        endY = (startY == 0) ? map->height - 1 : 0;
    } else {
        // Vertical river (west to east or east to west)
        startX = (randomChance(0.5f)) ? 0 : map->width - 1;
        startY = randomInt(map->height / 4, map->height * 3 / 4);
        endX = (startX == 0) ? map->width - 1 : 0;
        endY = randomInt(map->height / 4, map->height * 3 / 4);
    }
    
    // Generate a winding path for the river
    PathPoint* riverPath = generateWindingPath(context, map, startX, startY, endX, endY);
    
    // Create the river with varying width
    int baseWidth = randomInt(2, 4);
    int length = riverPath->length;
    
    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
        int x = riverPath->points[i].x;
        int y = riverPath->points[i].y;
        
        // Vary river width along its length
        int width = baseWidth;
        if (i < length / 5 || i > length * 4 / 5) {
            width = baseWidth - 1; // Narrower at ends
        } else if (i > length * 2 / 5 && i < length * 3 / 5) {
            width = baseWidth + 1; // Wider in the middle
        }
        
        // Create water tiles in a circular pattern around path point
        for (int dy = -width; dy <= width; dy++) {
            for (int dx = -width; dx <= width; dx++) {
                if (dx*dx + dy*dy <= width*width) {
                    int nx = x + dx;
                    int ny = y + dy;
                    
                    if (isInBounds(map, nx, ny)) {
                        // Don't place water in rooms or corridors
                        if (!isCriticalPath(map, nx, ny)) {
                            map->tiles[ny][nx].type = TILE_WATER;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    // Free the path
    freePath(riverPath);
}
```

### Vegetation and Growth

Add flora and organic elements:

```c
void addVegetation(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Determine vegetation density based on dungeon level
    float vegetationDensity = 0.5f - (context->dungeonLevel * 0.03f);
    if (vegetationDensity < 0.1f) vegetationDensity = 0.1f;
    
    // Add vegetation clusters
    int clusterCount = randomInt(3, 8);
    for (int i = 0; i < clusterCount; i++) {
        // Find a suitable location for a vegetation cluster
        int centerX = randomInt(5, map->width - 5);
        int centerY = randomInt(5, map->height - 5);
        
        // Skip if center is not a floor tile
        if (map->tiles[centerY][centerX].type != TILE_FLOOR) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Create a vegetation cluster
        int radius = randomInt(3, 6);
        float density = vegetationDensity * randomFloat() * 0.5f + vegetationDensity * 0.5f;
        
        for (int y = centerY - radius; y <= centerY + radius; y++) {
            for (int x = centerX - radius; x <= centerX + radius; x++) {
                if (!isInBounds(map, x, y)) continue;
                
                // Only place vegetation on floor tiles
                if (map->tiles[y][x].type != TILE_FLOOR) continue;
                
                // Calculate distance from center
                float distance = sqrtf((x - centerX) * (x - centerX) + (y - centerY) * (y - centerY));
                if (distance > radius) continue;
                
                // Higher chance of vegetation near the center
                float chance = density * (1.0f - distance / radius);
                if (randomChance(chance)) {
                    // Choose vegetation type
                    if (randomChance(0.7f)) {
                        map->tiles[y][x].vegetation = VEG_GRASS;
                    } else if (randomChance(0.6f)) {
                        map->tiles[y][x].vegetation = VEG_FUNGI;
                    } else {
                        map->tiles[y][x].vegetation = VEG_FLOWER;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Entity Placement

### Monster Placement

Position monsters strategically:

```c
void placeMonsters(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Calculate base monster count based on dungeon level
    int baseMonsterCount = 5 + context->dungeonLevel;
    int variance = baseMonsterCount / 4;
    int monsterCount = baseMonsterCount + randomInt(-variance, variance);
    
    // Place monsters
    for (int i = 0; i < monsterCount; i++) {
        // Choose a monster type based on dungeon level
        MonsterType type = chooseMonsterType(context);
        
        // Find a suitable position
        int x, y;
        if (!findMonsterPlacement(context, map, type, &x, &y)) {
            continue; // Skip if no suitable position found
        }
        
        // Create and place the monster
        Monster* monster = createMonster(type);
        monster->x = x;
        monster->y = y;
        
        // Add to the map's monster list
        addMonsterToMap(map, monster);
    }
    
    // Place special monsters (bosses, unique entities)
    if (context->dungeonLevel % 5 == 0) {
        placeSpecialMonster(context, map);
    }
}

bool findMonsterPlacement(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map, 
                          MonsterType type, int* outX, int* outY) {
    // Different monster types have different placement requirements
    bool needsWater = (type == MONSTER_FISH || type == MONSTER_FROG);
    bool needsVegetation = (type == MONSTER_INSECT || type == MONSTER_FUNGUS);
    bool needsOpen = (type == MONSTER_FLYER || type == MONSTER_LARGE_BEAST);
    
    // Try to find a suitable position
    for (int attempts = 0; attempts < 50; attempts++) {
        int x = randomInt(1, map->width - 2);
        int y = randomInt(1, map->height - 2);
        
        Tile* tile = &map->tiles[y][x];
        
        // Basic requirements - must be a passable tile with no monster already
        if (!isTilePassable(tile) || tileHasMonster(map, x, y)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Check specific requirements
        if (needsWater && tile->type != TILE_WATER) {
            continue;
        }
        
        if (needsVegetation && tile->vegetation == VEG_NONE) {
            continue;
        }
        
        if (needsOpen && !hasOpenSpace(map, x, y, 3)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Found a suitable position
        *outX = x;
        *outY = y;
        return true;
    }
    
    // Couldn't find a suitable position, relax constraints
    for (int attempts = 0; attempts < 50; attempts++) {
        int x = randomInt(1, map->width - 2);
        int y = randomInt(1, map->height - 2);
        
        Tile* tile = &map->tiles[y][x];
        
        // Just check basic passability
        if (isTilePassable(tile) && !tileHasMonster(map, x, y)) {
            *outX = x;
            *outY = y;
            return true;
        }
    }
    
    return false; // Really couldn't find a place
}
```

### Item Placement

Distribute items throughout the dungeon:

```c
void placeItems(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Calculate base item count based on dungeon level
    int baseItemCount = 3 + (context->dungeonLevel / 2);
    int variance = baseItemCount / 3;
    int itemCount = baseItemCount + randomInt(-variance, variance);
    
    // Place regular items
    for (int i = 0; i < itemCount; i++) {
        // Choose an item type based on dungeon level
        ItemType type = chooseItemType(context);
        
        // Find a suitable position
        int x, y;
        if (!findItemPlacement(context, map, type, &x, &y)) {
            continue; // Skip if no suitable position found
        }
        
        // Create and place the item
        Item* item = createItem(type);
        item->x = x;
        item->y = y;
        
        // Add to the map's item list
        addItemToMap(map, item);
    }
    
    // Place special items (quest items, artifacts)
    if (shouldPlaceSpecialItem(context)) {
        placeSpecialItem(context, map);
    }
}

bool findItemPlacement(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map, 
                       ItemType type, int* outX, int* outY) {
    // Different item types have different placement requirements
    bool needsContainer = (type == ITEM_GOLD || type == ITEM_GEM);
    bool needsWall = (type == ITEM_RUNE || type == ITEM_WALL_MOUNT);
    bool needsWater = (type == ITEM_POTION && randomChance(0.2f));
    
    // Try to find a suitable position
    for (int attempts = 0; attempts < 50; attempts++) {
        int x = randomInt(1, map->width - 2);
        int y = randomInt(1, map->height - 2);
        
        Tile* tile = &map->tiles[y][x];
        
        // Basic requirements - must be a valid tile with no item already
        if (tileHasItem(map, x, y)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Check specific requirements
        if (needsContainer && !tileHasContainer(tile)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        if (needsWall && !adjacentToWall(map, x, y)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        if (needsWater && tile->type != TILE_WATER) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Most items should be on passable terrain
        if (!needsWall && !isTilePassable(tile)) {
            continue;
        }
        
        // Found a suitable position
        *outX = x;
        *outY = y;
        return true;
    }
    
    // Couldn't find a suitable position, relax constraints
    for (int attempts = 0; attempts < 50; attempts++) {
        int x = randomInt(1, map->width - 2);
        int y = randomInt(1, map->height - 2);
        
        Tile* tile = &map->tiles[y][x];
        
        // Just check basic requirements
        if (isTilePassable(tile) && !tileHasItem(map, x, y)) {
            *outX = x;
            *outY = y;
            return true;
        }
    }
    
    return false; // Really couldn't find a place
}
```

## Special Feature Generation

### Traps and Hazards

Add dangerous elements to the dungeon:

```c
void placeTrapHazards(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Determine trap count based on dungeon level
    int trapCount = 2 + (context->dungeonLevel / 3);
    
    // Place traps
    for (int i = 0; i < trapCount; i++) {
        // Choose a trap type
        TrapType type = chooseTrapType(context);
        
        // Find a suitable position
        int x, y;
        if (!findTrapPlacement(context, map, type, &x, &y)) {
            continue; // Skip if no suitable position found
        }
        
        // Create and place the trap
        Trap* trap = createTrap(type);
        trap->x = x;
        trap->y = y;
        trap->visible = randomChance(0.2f); // Most traps start hidden
        
        // Add to the map's trap list
        addTrapToMap(map, trap);
    }
}

TrapType chooseTrapType(DungeonGenContext* context) {
    // Trap distribution changes based on dungeon level
    int level = context->dungeonLevel;
    
    // Simple traps are more common at early levels
    if (level < 5) {
        if (randomChance(0.7f)) {
            return TRAP_PIT;
        } else if (randomChance(0.6f)) {
            return TRAP_DART;
        } else {
            return TRAP_ALARM;
        }
    } 
    // Mid-level traps
    else if (level < 10) {
        if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_PIT;
        } else if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_DART;
        } else if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_POISON_GAS;
        } else {
            return TRAP_TELEPORT;
        }
    }
    // High-level traps
    else {
        if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_POISON_GAS;
        } else if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_TELEPORT;
        } else if (randomChance(0.3f)) {
            return TRAP_PARALYSIS;
        } else {
            return TRAP_SUMMONING;
        }
    }
}
```

### Special Rooms

Create unique and memorable room encounters:

```c
void addSpecialRooms(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Determine if this level should have a special room
    if (!shouldHaveSpecialRoom(context)) {
        return;
    }
    
    // Choose a special room type
    SpecialRoomType type = chooseSpecialRoomType(context);
    
    // Create the special room
    switch (type) {
        case SPECIAL_ROOM_VAULT:
            createVaultRoom(context, map);
            break;
        case SPECIAL_ROOM_LIBRARY:
            createLibraryRoom(context, map);
            break;
        case SPECIAL_ROOM_ALTAR:
            createAltarRoom(context, map);
            break;
        case SPECIAL_ROOM_GARDEN:
            createGardenRoom(context, map);
            break;
        case SPECIAL_ROOM_ARENA:
            createArenaRoom(context, map);
            break;
    }
}

void createVaultRoom(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Find a suitable location for the vault
    int width = randomInt(8, 12);
    int height = randomInt(8, 12);
    int x, y;
    
    if (!findRoomPlacement(map, width, height, &x, &y)) {
        return; // Can't place the vault
    }
    
    // Create a reinforced room
    for (int dy = 0; dy < height; dy++) {
        for (int dx = 0; dx < width; dx++) {
            int nx = x + dx;
            int ny = y + dy;
            
            if (dx == 0 || dx == width - 1 || dy == 0 || dy == height - 1) {
                // Reinforced walls around the perimeter
                map->tiles[ny][nx].type = TILE_WALL_REINFORCED;
            } else {
                // Floor inside
                map->tiles[ny][nx].type = TILE_FLOOR;
            }
        }
    }
    
    // Add a locked door
    int doorX = x + randomInt(1, width - 2);
    int doorY = y + randomInt(1, height - 2);
    
    // Place door on a wall
    if (randomChance(0.5f)) {
        doorX = (randomChance(0.5f)) ? x : x + width - 1;
    } else {
        doorY = (randomChance(0.5f)) ? y : y + height - 1;
    }
    
    map->tiles[doorY][doorX].type = TILE_DOOR_LOCKED;
    
    // Place valuable items inside the vault
    int itemCount = randomInt(3, 6);
    for (int i = 0; i < itemCount; i++) {
        int itemX = x + randomInt(1, width - 2);
        int itemY = y + randomInt(1, height - 2);
        
        ItemType type = chooseValuableItemType(context);
        Item* item = createItem(type);
        item->x = itemX;
        item->y = itemY;
        
        addItemToMap(map, item);
    }
    
    // Maybe add a trap or guardian
    if (randomChance(0.7f)) {
        int guardX = x + randomInt(1, width - 2);
        int guardY = y + randomInt(1, height - 2);
        
        if (randomChance(0.6f)) {
            // Add a powerful monster as guardian
            Monster* guardian = createMonster(MONSTER_VAULT_GUARDIAN);
            guardian->x = guardX;
            guardian->y = guardY;
            addMonsterToMap(map, guardian);
        } else {
            // Add a dangerous trap
            Trap* trap = createTrap(TRAP_PARALYSIS);
            trap->x = guardX;
            trap->y = guardY;
            trap->visible = false;
            addTrapToMap(map, trap);
        }
    }
}
```

## Testing and Validation

### Map Validation

Ensure the generated map meets design requirements:

```c
bool validateDungeonMap(DungeonMap* map) {
    // Check if the map has a valid player start
    bool hasPlayerStart = false;
    bool hasExit = false;
    
    // Check if the map is fully connected
    bool isConnected = checkMapConnectivity(map);
    
    // Check for basic features
    for (int y = 0; y < map->height; y++) {
        for (int x = 0; x < map->width; x++) {
            Tile* tile = &map->tiles[y][x];
            
            if (tile->type == TILE_ENTRANCE) {
                hasPlayerStart = true;
            } else if (tile->type == TILE_EXIT) {
                hasExit = true;
            }
        }
    }
    
    // A valid map must have:
    // 1. A player start point
    // 2. An exit
    // 3. Full connectivity between start and exit
    return hasPlayerStart && hasExit && isConnected;
}

bool checkMapConnectivity(DungeonMap* map) {
    // Find player start position
    int startX = -1, startY = -1;
    for (int y = 0; y < map->height; y++) {
        for (int x = 0; x < map->width; x++) {
            if (map->tiles[y][x].type == TILE_ENTRANCE) {
                startX = x;
                startY = y;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (startX != -1) break;
    }
    
    if (startX == -1) return false; // No start found
    
    // Use flood fill to check connectivity
    bool** visited = allocateBooleanGrid(map->width, map->height);
    if (!visited) return false;
    
    floodFill(map, visited, startX, startY);
    
    // Check if exit is reachable
    bool exitReachable = false;
    for (int y = 0; y < map->height; y++) {
        for (int x = 0; x < map->width; x++) {
            if (map->tiles[y][x].type == TILE_EXIT && visited[y][x]) {
                exitReachable = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (exitReachable) break;
    }
    
    // Free the visited grid
    freeBooleanGrid(visited, map->height);
    
    return exitReachable;
}
```

### Debugging Generation

Techniques for debugging procedural generation:

```c
void debugDungeonGeneration(DungeonGenContext* context, DungeonMap* map) {
    // Log generation parameters
    printf("Generating dungeon with seed: %u, level: %d\n", context->seed, context->dungeonLevel);
    
    // Create a visual representation of the map
    char** visualMap = createVisualMap(map);
    if (!visualMap) return;
    
    // Output the visual map
    printf("Map representation:\n");
    for (int y = 0; y < map->height; y++) {
        printf("%s\n", visualMap[y]);
    }
    
    // Free the visual map
    for (int y = 0; y < map->height; y++) {
        free(visualMap[y]);
    }
    free(visualMap);
    
    // Log statistics about the map
    printf("Map statistics:\n");
    printf("- Rooms: %d\n", map->roomCount);
    printf("- Corridors: %d\n", map->corridorCount);
    printf("- Water tiles: %d\n", countTileType(map, TILE_WATER));
    printf("- Monsters: %d\n", map->monsterCount);
    printf("- Items: %d\n", map->itemCount);
    printf("- Traps: %d\n", map->trapCount);
    
    // Check map integrity
    bool isValid = validateDungeonMap(map);
    printf("Map validation: %s\n", isValid ? "PASSED" : "FAILED");
    
    if (!isValid) {
        // Log specific validation issues
        logMapValidationIssues(map);
    }
}
```

By following these guidelines, you can create rich, varied, and interesting procedural dungeons in BrogueMCP.